    { q: "What is 'alliteration'?", options: ["An extreme exaggeration", "The repetition of initial consonant sounds in nearby words", "A word imitating a sound", "A direct comparison between two things"], correct: 1, explanation: "Alliteration is the repetition of the same initial consonant sound in a series of nearby words." },
    { q: "Why might a writer use alliteration?", options: ["To make text harder to read on purpose", "To create rhythm, draw attention, or add a musical quality to writing", "Alliteration serves no purpose", "Only to confuse readers"], correct: 1, explanation: "Alliteration is often used to create rhythm, emphasis, or a memorable, musical quality in writing, common in poetry and advertising." }
