    { q: "Which of these is an example of onomatopoeia?", options: ["Happy", "Boom", "Quickly", "Beautiful"], correct: 1, explanation: "\"Boom\" imitates the sound of a loud explosion or impact, making it onomatopoeia." },
    { q: "Why do writers use onomatopoeia?", options: ["To make writing sound more vivid and realistic by mimicking actual sounds", "To confuse readers with strange words", "Onomatopoeia serves no purpose", "To avoid describing sounds at all"], correct: 0, explanation: "Onomatopoeia helps make writing more vivid and immersive by directly imitating the sounds being described." }
