    { q: "What characterizes 'first-person' point of view?", options: ["The narrator is an outside observer describing everyone using 'he' or 'she'", "The narrator is a character in the story, using 'I' or 'we'", "The narrator knows every character's thoughts", "There is no narrator at all"], correct: 1, explanation: "First-person point of view uses 'I' or 'we,' with the narrator being a character directly involved in the story." },
    { q: "What characterizes 'third-person omniscient' point of view?", options: ["The narrator only knows one character's thoughts", "The narrator knows the thoughts and feelings of multiple or all characters", "The story is told using 'I'", "There is no narration"], correct: 1, explanation: "Third-person omniscient narration allows the narrator to know and share the thoughts and feelings of multiple (or all) characters in the story." }
