    { q: "What does 'import' mean in trade?", options: ["Selling goods to another country", "Bringing goods or services into a country from abroad", "The same thing as an export", "A type of tax only"], correct: 1, explanation: "To 'import' means to bring goods or services into a country from another country, typically to sell or use domestically." },
    { q: "Why might a country choose to import goods that it could theoretically produce domestically?", options: ["Importing never makes economic sense", "It may be more cost-effective or efficient to import certain goods, based on factors like specialization and resource availability", "Countries are legally required to produce everything domestically", "Imports have no economic benefit ever"], correct: 1, explanation: "Countries often import goods when it's more cost-effective or efficient to do so, based on factors like specialization, resource availability, and comparative advantage." }
