    { q: "What is a common concern associated with monopolies?", options: ["Monopolies always benefit consumers with lower prices", "Without competition, a monopoly may charge higher prices or offer lower quality, since consumers have no alternative", "Monopolies have no potential downsides", "Monopolies always lead to more innovation than competitive markets"], correct: 1, explanation: "A common concern is that without competitive pressure, a monopoly may charge higher prices or provide lower quality, since consumers lack alternative options." },
    { q: "Why do many governments regulate or restrict monopolies through antitrust laws?", options: ["Governments never regulate monopolies", "To help promote competition and protect consumers from potential negative effects of a single dominant seller", "Antitrust laws serve no economic purpose", "Regulating monopolies always harms consumers"], correct: 1, explanation: "Many governments use antitrust laws to help promote market competition and protect consumers from the potential negative effects (like higher prices) of an unchecked, dominant monopoly." }
