    { q: "What is an 'oligopoly'?", options: ["A market with countless small sellers", "A market structure dominated by a small number of large sellers", "A market with a single seller (a monopoly)", "A market with no competition of any kind, but also no dominant sellers"], correct: 1, explanation: "An oligopoly is a market structure dominated by a small number of large sellers, who often have significant influence over prices and market conditions." },
    { q: "How does 'monopolistic competition' generally differ from perfect competition?", options: ["They are identical concepts", "In monopolistic competition, many sellers offer similar but slightly differentiated products, giving each some limited pricing power", "Monopolistic competition always involves only one seller", "There is no meaningful difference between the two"], correct: 1, explanation: "In monopolistic competition, many sellers offer similar but not identical products (like different brands of restaurants), giving each seller some limited ability to set prices, unlike in perfect competition." }
