    { q: "What is the formula for permutations, nPr, used to calculate the number of ways to arrange r items chosen from n total items (where order matters)?", options: ["n! / r!", "n! / (n-r)!", "n! × r!", "r! / n!"], correct: 1, explanation: "The permutations formula is nPr = n! / (n-r)!, which calculates the number of ordered arrangements of r items chosen from n total items." },
    { q: "Using the permutations formula, how many ways can you choose and arrange 2 people (in order) from a group of 4 people?", options: ["6", "8", "12", "24"], correct: 2, explanation: "Using nPr = n!/(n-r)!: 4P2 = 4!/(4-2)! = 4!/2! = 24/2 = 12." },
    { q: "How many ways can 1st, 2nd, and 3rd place medals be awarded among 5 competitors?", options: ["15", "60", "125", "10"], correct: 1, explanation: "This is a permutation since order matters (1st, 2nd, 3rd are different): 5P3 = 5!/(5-3)! = 5!/2! = 120/2 = 60." }
