          { q: "A computer has a very fast processor but only a small amount of RAM. What is a likely consequence when running multiple demanding programs at once?", options: ["The computer will run every program instantly with no issues", "The system may struggle to keep up and could slow down or become unresponsive, since RAM is needed for actively running tasks", "The processor speed becomes completely irrelevant in this situation", "This combination has no effect on performance"], correct: 1, explanation: "With only a small amount of RAM, the system may struggle to keep up with multiple demanding programs running simultaneously, since RAM is needed to temporarily hold data for actively running tasks, regardless of how fast the processor is." }
