    { q: "Which of these is a common example of a 'second factor' used in two-factor authentication?", options: ["Simply typing your password a second time", "A one-time code sent via text message or generated by an authenticator app", "Using a shorter, simpler password", "Sharing your password with a trusted friend"], correct: 1, explanation: "A common example of a second factor is a one-time code sent via text message or generated by a dedicated authenticator app, which changes periodically and is separate from your password." }
