    { q: "What is 'pattern recognition,' as it relates to programming and problem-solving?", options: ["A term with no relevance to programming", "Identifying similarities or recurring trends within a problem, which can help find a general solution or approach", "Randomly guessing at a solution with no analysis involved", "A type of programming language syntax error"], correct: 1, explanation: "Pattern recognition involves identifying similarities or recurring trends within a problem, which can help programmers find a more general, reusable solution or approach, rather than solving each specific case separately." },
    { q: "Why is pattern recognition considered a useful skill for programmers?", options: ["Pattern recognition has no practical benefit for programming", "Recognizing similar patterns across different problems can allow programmers to apply similar, previously successful solutions or approaches", "Pattern recognition only applies to a single, extremely narrow class of unrelated problems", "This skill is exclusively relevant outside of any programming context"], correct: 1, explanation: "Pattern recognition is useful because recognizing similar patterns across different problems can allow programmers to apply similar, previously successful solutions or approaches, rather than needing to solve each new problem completely from scratch." },
    { q: "If a programmer notices that several different tasks all involve repeating an action a specific number of times, what programming concept might this pattern suggest using?", options: ["This pattern suggests using a completely unrelated programming concept", "A loop, since the underlying pattern of repeated actions matches what loops are generally designed to handle", "This pattern has no relevant connection to any specific programming concept", "A single, one-time function call with absolutely no repetition involved"], correct: 1, explanation: "Recognizing a pattern of needing to repeat an action a specific number of times suggests that a loop would be an appropriate programming concept to apply, since loops are specifically designed to handle this kind of repeated action." }
